<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);Nullable</WarningsAsErrors>

    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

    <Authors>Haik Asatryan</Authors>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>

    <PackageIcon>resultcrafter-icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <Version>3.1.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Added: field error codes, so a client can show validation errors in its own language. A validation 400 now carries errorCodes next to errors: the same keys, and for each message a { code, args } entry at the same index; errors keeps its exact shape, and errorCodes is left out when no field error has a code or args. New FieldError type (message, optional code, typed args through With) and Error.BadRequest(IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, FieldError[]&gt;) for field errors built in a handler; Error.FieldErrors reads them back. ResultCrafter.FluentValidation and WithValidation&lt;T&gt;() fill the code from each failure's ErrorCode (FluentValidation's validator name, such as NotEmptyValidator, when the rule sets none) and the rule's limits as args (minLength, maxLength when the rule has a maximum, from, to, expectedPrecision, expectedScale, and a comparisonValue that is neither a string nor another property); the attempted value is never copied. ProblemResponse documents errorCodes in OpenAPI (new FieldErrorCode schema type). Changed: two validation errors with the same messages but different codes or args are no longer equal. Error.BadRequest(IReadOnlyDictionary&lt;string, string[]&gt;) now throws ArgumentException for a null message instead of sending JSON null, which the errors schema does not allow. Update all ResultCrafter packages together: an older package next to a 3.1 one drops errorCodes and sends the 3.0 body. Guide: https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter/blob/main/docs/guide.md#field-error-codes</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- Build quality -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Source/symbols -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Each package packs the README next to its csproj: nuget.org shows raw HTML as text and blanks relative links,
       so the GitHub README at the root cannot be reused there. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)assets/resultcrafter-icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
